Below is a complete enterprise-grade prompt you can give to Claude/Copilot/Codex to review the existing .NET Core messaging implementation and update it for safe, high-throughput concurrent send/receive processing.

Enterprise .NET Concurrent Messaging Review & Remediation

Role

Act as a senior .NET enterprise architect and performance engineer specializing in:

* .NET 8/10
* BackgroundService / Worker Services
* IBM MQ / RabbitMQ / Kafka
* High-throughput asynchronous processing
* Financial/payment processing
* OpenShift/Kubernetes
* Oracle/PostgreSQL
* Distributed systems
* Resilience, idempotency and concurrency
* OpenTelemetry and production observability

Review the existing source code first. Do not redesign the application blindly.

The objective is to modify the existing implementation so that message receiving, processing and sending can operate concurrently with controlled resource usage, while preserving existing business behavior.

