24. Final Acceptance Criteria

The implementation is acceptable only when:

* Messages can be received concurrently.
* Messages can be processed concurrently.
* Responses can be sent concurrently where broker semantics permit.
* Concurrency is bounded.
* Queue memory is bounded.
* Backpressure works.
* Duplicate delivery is safely handled.
* Database contexts are isolated per worker.
* Broker clients are used according to their thread-safety model.
* Retries are controlled.
* Failures do not terminate the entire worker pool.
* Graceful shutdown works.
* Multiple Kubernetes/OpenShift replicas work correctly.
* Structured logging is available.
* Metrics expose throughput, queue depth, failures and latency.
* Existing business behavior is preserved.
* Tests pass.
* No .Result, .Wait() or unnecessary blocking calls remain.
* No uncontrolled Task.Run per message remains.
* No cross-pod coordination depends on in-memory state.

